{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical","id":944726,"title":"[2E] Basic vs Complex Refinements \u2013 Illogical","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-05T23:08:28-07:00","id":944726,"title":"[2E] Basic vs Complex Refinements \u2013 Illogical","content":"Reading Chapter Two of new corebook, I get to the section telling about Pilgrimage and Refinements. And there I discover one great setting illogical gap \u2013 Complex Refinements. Text says this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p. 80</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complex Refinements on the other hand do not come so naturally, much as not every human is a poet or can speak a second language. Prometheans believe that complex Refinements were created by Prometheans themselves long ago. In uncovering these new paths, the ancient Pilgrims unlocked their potential in Azoth itself, thus granting all Prometheans the potential to learn them. Such an effort requires a teacher though, an instructional tome, or an Athanor. Azoth alone isn\u2019t enough for a Promethean to adopt a complex Refinement, but it can help in finding an instructor.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Complex Refinements were uncovered some time in distant past, they <i>surel</i>y can be uncovered ones more now, by lonely Created. I can agree they can be <i>much easier</i> to learn from teacher, but <b>should not b</b><b>e</b> <b>limited</b> only to him and Pyros touched items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T23:23:52-07:00","id":944733,"title":"","content":"We didn't just start knowing how to work iron. We started with wood, then stone, then various metals to bronze, and then to iron.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible for an individual to learn, per se, but you are asking them to learn a complex material/spiritual alchemical refinement that took centuries of work for other Prometheans to finally hammer into a discernable- usable -form, without outside help. Just, you know, bam- be the cause of an Industrial Revolution in the span of your life time.<br /> <br /> Basically, they'd have to be the Promethean equivalent of the love child of Buddha and Tesla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-06-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T23:43:00-07:00","id":944737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944733#post944733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We didn't just start knowing how to work iron. We started with wood, then stone, then various metals to bronze, and then to iron.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible for an individual to learn, per se, but you are asking them to learn a complex material/spiritual alchemical refinement that took centuries of work for other Prometheans to finally hammer into a discernable- usable -form, without outside help. Just, you know, bam- be the cause of an Industrial Revolution in the span of your life time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what the first Prometheans to unlock these refinements did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T23:58:22-07:00","id":944740,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I look over Refinements themselves. If you were starting at Aurum to mimic humans and could not work with that there is logical step to look over on idea of mimicking monsters - and by this going to Argentum. Aes, literally, points as related to Ferrum and Stannum ( look in sidebar on page 81 ). Mercurius is logical next step after Plumbum.<br /> <br /> I can agree you should not start with Complex ( well, most of time at least ), but saying that character on itself cannot go after them when ended or stopped some Basic Refinements? It's artificial limitation that is illogical to setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:14:46-07:00","id":944743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944737#post944737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that what the first Prometheans to unlock these refinements did?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's too cool for PCs to do, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:46:24-07:00","id":944749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944740#post944740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I look over Refinements themselves. If you were starting at Aurum to mimic humans and could not work with that there is logical step to look over on idea of mimicking monsters - and by this going to Argentum. Aes, literally, points as related to Ferrum and Stannum ( look in sidebar on page 81 ). Mercurius is logical next step after Plumbum.<br /> <br /> I can agree you should not start with Complex ( well, most of time at least ), but saying that character on itself cannot go after them when ended or stopped some Basic Refinements? It's artificial limitation that is illogical to setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) I do not know why you keep using an emote that is literally named confused for consternation.<br /> <br /> 2) Keep in mind that you have the benefit of a human perspective. You are looking down from the top of the mountain. Prometheans do not have that luxury.<br /> <br /> 3) Keep in mind that all forms of philosophy and technological advancement have taken time to be refined over generations, some trains of thought or production practices being literally impossible for earlier civilizations. In a fit of irony for our example, consider both transhumanism and the computer-both of these would be literally impossible things from a bronze age human to comprehend. Now keep in mind that philosophy and form are one in the same for the Promethean, so an advancement in one is obviously an advancement in the other, or the entire thing's fucked, and then remember that, once again, Prometheans do not enjoy the same perspective as humans do.<br /> <br /> 3) Argentum is actually a crystal clear example of why the Complex Refinements are not as intrinsically intuitive as the Basic Refinements and probably came about as the result of at least several centuries of Prometheans asking questions, hammering on concepts and pondering on executions. I mean, seriously-who the fuck would ever think you can learn about humanity from a demon or an Abyssal manifestation? Hell, before even asking that, you would need an environment that facilitated such thoughts, one that allowed for reflection, and then reflection by contrast, and then one that regards monstrous incarnation to express humanity rather than the world. All of that alone <i>for humans</i> actually took a longer time than most think. THen you have Prometheans, who <i>are those monsters</i>, and have them observe and realize those things <i>for themselves</i> and then begin building the details, the alchemic processes that manifest the theory both inside and out, then test them and make note of where they failed and succeeded, and then refine the process until you have the package we know today.<br /> <br /> Phosphorum would have been easy for Prometheans to disregard for ages as merely manifesting a death wish to stave off the boredom and ennui, until a bunch of people dug deep and found the roots of the surfaces in Ephemerality.<br /> Mercurius just seems like wasting time on a more specific subject the Originists already cover, because fuck if Pyros specifically is going matter when you're human, until Prometheans realized it might and that the principles around Pyros certainly do.<br /> Aes literally just reads as &quot;Friendship is Magic&quot; until you begin understanding the definition of humanity by their relations and the deeper ramifications of that in terms of power, authority, trust, alienation, etc, etc.<br /> Cobalus reads as a hoity-toity temper tantrum that as least the Stannum have the good grace to be honest about until you realized that perfection lies in the imperfection, that beauty and interest is in the flaws, and the vast myriad of other things that go into Cobalt.<br /> <br /> And all of that is a ridiculously simplified version of the myriad of things going on with each of them, and that's understood by someone who has the benefit of directly understanding and being involved with the very thing Prometheans are literally trying to grasp in both a material and spiritual sense (as in, it's not a thing you can just know, but a thing you have to experience), and <i>none </i>of that includes the fact that they literally have to try every tenet and thought as an actual alchemical balance that sits pretty on their nature.<br /> <br /> No. It's not simple. It only seems simple to you because you're human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:57:46-07:00","id":944751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944743#post944743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's too cool for PCs to do, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer to many things you will see in <b>PtC</b> 2E corebook... What a pitty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:12:40-07:00","id":944828,"title":"","content":"Here's a relevant video.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=g-KuigAQFp4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=g-KuigAQFp4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=g-KuigAQFp4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=g-KuigAQFp4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nothing revolutionary is ever invented by one person in one lifetime. These things are the result of generations of findings built upon one another until it reaches a critical mass.<br /> <br /> Yes, new Refinements can be developed. No, one character can't develop a new refinement single-handedly over the time span of a single story. It might make a cool core idea of a whole chronicle, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:16:27-07:00","id":944830,"title":"","content":"The easier answer is that even those Prometheans who originally created the Complex Refinements didn't start from scratch: they had mentors and studied what came before and built on those things. They didn't just say &quot;I want a new Refinement, I'll get to work on that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, Complex Refinements were originally developed over several Promethean lifetimes of study and refinement, not a sudden burst of insight.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Dang, Charlaquin'd!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:38:40-07:00","id":944839,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is a really strange place for this complaint to suddenly pop up too. Like, Coils of the Dragon are invented by vampires, but I've never seen anyone complain that players can't just make new Coils whenever they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T07:54:32-07:00","id":944848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944830#post944830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easier answer is that even those Prometheans who originally created the Complex Refinements didn't start from scratch: they had mentors and studied what came before and built on those things. They didn't just say &quot;I want a new Refinement, I'll get to work on that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, Complex Refinements were originally developed over several Promethean lifetimes of study and refinement, not a sudden burst of insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>But those Complex creators still needed to be Refinement participants in the first place, as philosophy is physical change in <b>Promethean</b>. In other words, to create lore on Argentum, you <b><i>need</i></b> to be on Argentum in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>If no Promethean can be on Refinement before creation, we <i>cannot </i>have creators on it, so no creation ( i.e. Refinements )!</b> ( It's logical <b>contradiction</b>. )<br /> <br /> Example - Created Jacob is ancient master that created Argentum for Azothic Memory, centuries ago. To do this, Jacob needed to spend years of study on other monsters of universe - time he spend on creating new Refinement. But in the doing so, he <i>was</i> participant of what later come to be named Argentum Refinement, as his transformation resolve about monsters in first place. That he did not called it Argentum (yet) do not change the fact that he lived by observing and emulating monsters in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:17:01-07:00","id":944853,"title":"","content":"Doing a thing as part of your pilgrimage doesn't automatically make that thing a Refinement, though. I'm sure lots of Prometheans over the generations studied various supernatural creatures to gain insight into what made them <i>not</i> human, long before it was codified as a Refinement. Some of them may have taken notes on their findings. Some of them may have passed on those notes in the form of Athanors. Some who studied the practice probably experimented with Transmutations based on the findings of those who came before them, and after a few generations of this, it was probably whittled down to the set that is part of Argentum today. Some who studied it probably experimented with different Roles related to the study of the supernatural until it was eventually found that the three we see today were the most successful. And at some point, someone gave a name to the practice.<br /> <br /> The point is, significant inventions aren't made by individuals in isolation. Invention is an ongoing process that occurs over decades, centuries, and millennia. If you want to allow your characters to take part in the process of inventing a new Refinement, great! Figure out what groundwork has already been laid down by those who came before and have them add their own work onto that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:37:11-07:00","id":944863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944733#post944733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We didn't just start knowing how to work iron. We started with wood, then stone, then various metals to bronze, and then to iron.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible for an individual to learn, per se, but you are asking them to learn a complex material/spiritual alchemical refinement that took centuries of work for other Prometheans to finally hammer into a discernable- usable -form, without outside help. Just, you know, bam- be the cause of an Industrial Revolution in the span of your life time.<br /> <br /> Basically, they'd have to be the Promethean equivalent of the love child of Buddha and Tesla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually this kind of thing is best represented through the culturally context-sensitive interplay of creativity and tradition. You are right that you can only jump the gap to working with stone if you already have a tradition of working with wood. But you must also be creative enough to see beyond the tradition of working with wood. Like most things, this should really be left for individual story-tellers and players to agree upon. Because context will matter a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:41:14-07:00","id":944866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944853#post944853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, significant inventions aren't made by individuals in isolation. Invention is an ongoing process that occurs over decades, centuries, and millennia. If you want to allow your characters to take part in the process of inventing a new Refinement, great! Figure out what groundwork has already been laid down by those who came before and have them add their own work onto that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of depends on how one defines invention and isolation. Do you need some base knowledge? Yes. Are most inventions actually created in isolation? Also yes. But again, I think these kinds of interactions are probably outside of the scope of rules beyond, &quot;it costs more to figure this out on your own&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:44:45-07:00","id":944869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944853#post944853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing a thing as part of your pilgrimage doesn't automatically make that thing a Refinement, though. I'm sure lots of Prometheans over the generations studied various supernatural creatures to gain insight into what made them <i>not</i> human, long before it was codified as a Refinement. Some of them may have taken notes on their findings. Some of them may have passed on those notes in the form of Athanors. Some who studied the practice probably experimented with Transmutations based on the findings of those who came before them, and after a few generations of this, it was probably whittled down to the set that is part of Argentum today. Some who studied it probably experimented with different Roles related to the study of the supernatural until it was eventually found that the three we see today were the most successful. And at some point, someone gave a name to the practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the problem you seems to miss - Refinements <b><i>are</i></b> acts of it. As much as Refinements are philosophy, they are also physical changes that have real effect on Created - because they are Alchemy 'of mind and spirit', entwine with one another by Divine Fire. Mimic going after Aurum is doing that <i>because</i> he is trying to understand humans <i>right now </i>or try to blend with humans, not because he read about it on cave wall. More, he can universally points that this \u2018tactic\u2019 works, as he get\u2019s <i>powers</i> that are related to it \u2013 if he would do something \u2018wrong\u2019 he would not get Transmutations.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, to start participating in any Refinement you need idea what to do with your Promethean life OR Role in it ( acting like ) OR lore of Refinement OR uncover Transmutations of it OR some teacher of it ( that gives you nice package of previous elements ).</b> And all the rest is filled by Azothic Memory for once created Refinements, as character \u2018remembers\u2019 how to work Refinement from previous generations of Created.<br /> <br /> If your assessment were true \u2013 <b>that you need to get ALL of mentioned by me elements \u2013 there would be <i>no</i> alone Created on any Basic Refinement</b> - as they would not have information about lore, Transmutations or Roles that are part of it to start Refinement going straight \u2018from slab\u2019, like corebook is defining it. No alone spontaneous Mimics, no self-discovered Titans just after hours or days of living. As core points it is other way, your assessment must be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:51:57-07:00","id":944875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944866#post944866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of depends on how one defines invention and isolation. Do you need some base knowledge? Yes. Are most inventions actually created in isolation? Also yes. But again, I think these kinds of interactions are probably outside of the scope of rules beyond, &amp;quot;it costs more to figure this out on your own&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, inventions aren't made in a vacuum. They are built upon the success of previous inventions, which themselves are built upon the success of previous inventions, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:59:17-07:00","id":944878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944869#post944869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is the problem you seems to miss - Refinements <b><i>are</i></b> acts of it. As much as Refinements are philosophy, they are also physical changes that have real effect on Created - because they are Alchemy 'of mind and spirit', entwine with one another by Divine Fire. Mimic going after Aurum is doing that <i>because</i> he is trying to understand humans <i>right now </i>or try to blend with humans, not because he read about it on cave wall. More, he can universally points that this \u2018tactic\u2019 works, as he get\u2019s <i>powers</i> that are related to it \u2013 if he would do something \u2018wrong\u2019 he would not get Transmutations.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, to start participating in any Refinement you need idea what to do with your Promethean life OR Role in it ( acting like ) OR lore of Refinement OR uncover Transmutations of it OR some teacher of it ( that gives you nice package of previous elements ).</b> And all the rest is filled by Azothic Memory for once created Refinements, as character \u2018remembers\u2019 how to work Refinement from previous generations of Created.<br /> <br /> If your assessment were true \u2013 <b>that you need to get ALL of mentioned by me elements \u2013 there would be <i>no</i> alone Created on any Basic Refinement</b> - as they would not have information about lore, Transmutations or Roles that are part of it to start Refinement going straight \u2018from slab\u2019, like corebook is defining it. No alone spontaneous Mimics, no self-discovered Titans just after hours or days of living. As core points it is other way, your assessment must be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how <i>Basic</i> Refinements work. That's not how <i>Complex</i> Refinements (you know, the ones that can be invented) work. They are not a part of every Promethean's Azothic memory, they have to be learned, either by a mentor or by an Athanor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:00:18-07:00","id":944879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944875#post944875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean is, inventions aren't made in a vacuum. They are built upon the success of previous inventions, which themselves are built upon the success of previous inventions, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is only partially true. Humans are very very good at the reinventing the wheel game. Trust me, I see this in CS all the time. I think there's a lot of discounting the exceptions that make the rules but again, I think adding too many rules are out of scope for games like these. Basically you're saying it's impossible for players to play characters that are savants and geniuses which kind of detracts from them being the main characters of the story... :/<br /> <br /> Personally this isn't a position I would take. This kind of thing needs to be left to individual storytellers and players to agree upon. Invention after all is a very aspirational thing. <br /> <br /> Note that I don't think anyone's arguing that this needs to be easy. Merely possible through multiple routes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:09:41-07:00","id":944883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944878#post944878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how <i>Basic</i> Refinements work. That's not how <i>Complex</i> Refinements (you know, the ones that can be invented) work. They are not a part of every Promethean's Azothic memory, they have to be learned, either by a mentor or by an Athanor.</div> </div> </div> </div>As to my point is simple - If your new Transmutations works - it's Refinement. If your now way of life works as Role and generate Milestones and/or Wastelands - it's Refinement. Prometheans can <i>objectively </i>measure if their actions are or aren't Refinements because of Azoth.<br /> <br /> <b>Creators of Refinements maybe needed years of study to prove those and codifying in to lore ( and Azothic Memory ), but from mechanical stand point, Created can now assert if his actions are and aren't Refinements <i>in matter of weeks. </i></b>Basic or Complex one.<br /> <br /> And to counter your next point to rise - one Created will know those symptoms, as he needed to dwell in at least one Basic Refinement before starting Complex one. So he can self asses if he is doing Refinement or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:22:53-07:00","id":944890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944879#post944879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only partially true. Humans are very very good at the reinventing the wheel game. Trust me, I see this in CS all the time. I think there's a lot of discounting the exceptions that make the rules but again, I think adding too many rules are out of scope for games like these. Basically you're saying it's impossible for players to play characters that are savants and geniuses which kind of detracts from them being the main characters of the story... :/<br /> <br /> Personally this isn't a position I would take. This kind of thing needs to be left to individual storytellers and players to agree upon. Invention after all is a very aspirational thing. <br /> <br /> Note that I don't think anyone's arguing that this needs to be easy. Merely possible through multiple routes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying at all. I said the idea of creating a new Refinement would make a cool seed for a Chronicle. I just don't think it's the kind of thing that's possible in the course of a single Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:27:05-07:00","id":944894,"title":"","content":"Actually, you know what? I don't have the patience to argue about whether or not there's a problem. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, you obviously feel there is and you're not going to be convinced otherwise. So how do you propose fixing it? What do you want development of new Refinements to look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:27:34-07:00","id":944895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944890#post944890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what I'm saying at all. I said the idea of creating a new Refinement would make a cool seed for a Chronicle. I just don't think it's the kind of thing that's possible in the course of a single Story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I didn't get that from your previous text. But now that you state it this way, agree 100%. (Me being a stingy bastard might make it the B-story of multiple Chronicles because invention is hard.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:40:26-07:00","id":944906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944894#post944894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, you obviously feel there is and you're not going to be convinced otherwise. So how do you propose fixing it? What do you want development of new Refinements to look like?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>No <i>need</i> for mentor with Complex Refinements. Only maybe marking teacher makes it <u>easier</u> with one.</b> From logical stand point, in matter of weeks each Created can self asses if he is doing good on Pilgrimage. Other Promethean teaching on Refinement or Athanor of it can shorten this time considerably.<br /> <br /> As to looking for totally <b><i>new</i></b> Refinements - those that are <b>not</b> mentioned in corebook - experimenting probably takes a bit more, but I think in matter of few months character can point if she makes some progress on Pilgrimage. She may not have name for it, but it <i>will</i> show some fruits, like new Transmutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:43:41-07:00","id":944908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944895#post944895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I didn't get that from your previous text. But now that you state it this way, agree 100%. (Me being a stingy bastard might make it the B-story of multiple Chronicles because invention is hard.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. I imagine you probably skimmed past this part of my first post in the thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944828#post944828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, new Refinements can be developed. No, one character can't develop a new refinement single-handedly over the time span of a single story. It might make a cool core idea of a whole chronicle, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:45:10-07:00","id":944909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944906#post944906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>No <i>need</i> for mentor with Complex Refinements. Only maybe marking teacher makes it <u>easier</u> with one.</b> From logical stand point, in matter of weeks each Created can self asses if he is doing good on Pilgrimage. Other Promethean teaching on Refinement or Athanor of it can shorten this time considerably.<br /> <br /> As to looking for totally <b><i>new</i></b> Refinements - those that are <b>not</b> mentioned in corebook - experimenting probably takes a bit more, but I think in matter of few months character can point if she makes some progress on Pilgrimage. She may not have name for it, but it <i>will</i> show some fruits, like new Transmutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, go ahead and run your games that way then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:47:35-07:00","id":944911,"title":"","content":"Simply pissing me a bit that is illogical barrier on rules about Complex Refinements. Mentor is no truly needed - it's certainly <i>helpful</i>, but rules are limiting players and characters choice. Needlessly and illogically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:59:21-07:00","id":944917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944911#post944911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply pissing me a bit that is illogical barrier on rules about Complex Refinements. Mentor is no truly needed - it's certainly <i>helpful</i>, but rules are limiting players and characters choice. Needlessly and illogically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with you that it's illogical, and evidently neither do the writers or the developer. But that's fine, you know exactly how you want it to work, so just make it work that way in your games and move on instead of wasting your own energy being pissed off about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:06:34-07:00","id":944921,"title":"","content":"Maybe model it after Mage and it's solution to &quot;Self Taught Legacies vs Mentored Legacies&quot;? This whole thing sounds similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:27:04-07:00","id":944930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944743#post944743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's too cool for PCs to do, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This <b>IS</b> a valid point, in metagame perspective, but from an in-game side, I'd offer as well: Azoth doesn't make sense, and that's WHY it's Azoth.<br /> <br /> Everything we know about how the phenomenon of Azoth, from the movement of Pyros to the actions of Qashmallim to the expressions of Azothic radiance, NONE of what the Divine Fire does or is makes sense to a scientist or natural philosopher or even the alchemic children of the Azothic Principle themselves. That the complex Refinements are very different from the 'base' Refinements ought \u2013 or really <b>MUST</b> to my way of seeing things \u2013 cause confusion to the Created as well as to anyone outside their experience. <br /> <br /> The invention of a Refinement doesn't fit with the way anything else is invented? Blame the impossible-to-fathom-ways of Azoth for that. You want a universal principle that cares one dingo's fig for cause-and-effect? Brother, you're looking for the God-Machine, I think. <br /> <br /> ...Of course, the metagame notion of not just dumping all of the Refinements together into one classification IS a great reason. The fact that the Pilgrimage demands mastering Refinements of more-than-one classification is kind of elegant from a game-design standpoint, especially when one considers that <b>Promethean: the Created</b> is the only Chronicles of Darkness game that has a built-in 'finish line' to it. There needs to be some way to balance the demands of story and the demands of mechanics. Further to this I'd add that, with this game even moreso than with others of the CofD, one is always able to change rules... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When reading this book, any time you see a declarative<br /> statement about the Created, please mentally append \u201cusually\u201d<br /> to the statement. Prometheans cannot sire or bear children\u2026<br /> usually. Prometheans cause Disquiet in human beings\u2026usually.<br /> Prometheans become human at the end of the Pilgrimage\u2026usually.<br /> <b>Promethean</b> relies on strange, unique circumstances and once-ina-<br /> billion occurrences, though, so if something happens in your<br /> chronicles that breaks the rules, that\u2019s entirely in keeping with the<br /> game\u2019s intent. (page 12) </div> </div> </div>Needless to say, your game's gonna figure out how any and all of this works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T11:54:23-07:00","id":944979,"title":"","content":"Worth noting is that the Basic Refinements are the sort of things that would alchemically just fit into a Promethean's frame-they have direct roots in the Promethean Condition. The Complex Refinements are no so similarly rooted, as they require a closer-to-human state of perspective/being, in that they require a Promethean to really stretch to create the alchemical reaction and flow that.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I find one big problem with this thread lies in the word &quot;illogical&quot;. Well, yeah, course it might be illogical. It's <i>alchemy</i>. Science and logic is a part of it, but it's not the sole tools of observation-it's as much an instinctual, spiritual process as it is ordered and observable. it's not enough to see and think a thing, you have to then figure out how to make those ideas transmute and transform- substantiate it through translating them into Transmutations, creating a place in the world with them vying transforming them into Roles, discovering the common base of how this all transforms into Vitriol-all of which the book points out can't just be done by sitting in a lab and pontificating about the nature of life, because of the nature of alchemy and these beings that pretty much are alchemy, who need to do and experience and discover these formulas for self-actualization.<br /> <br /> Of course it's not completely logical. It never was wholly logical. To try and understand it purely by logic is to miss half of the equation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:10:38-07:00","id":944991,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is nothing to get hackles up over. If you don't like it, change it. If you change it, consider the consequences. For example, you've taken what was a privileged, narrative-driven option and dropped the entry bar significantly. And maybe that's what you need for your game, but if tone going to go that far, you could just go whole hog and erase the distinction between basic and complex entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:14:27-07:00","id":944995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944921#post944921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe model it after Mage and it's solution to &quot;Self Taught Legacies vs Mentored Legacies&quot;? This whole thing sounds similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came to same conclusion few moments ago -<b> 'Self Taught Refinements' should be just a bit more difficult to get than 'Mentored'</b>. Just like in <b>Mage</b> most character will be mentored in Legacy, so most Created will learn Complex Refinements from teach or Athanor ( clear analogy to Daimonomicons ). Still, those that putted time and thought on their own should be able to create / take existing Refinement on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944726-2e-basic-vs-complex-refinements-\u2013-illogical?p=944991#post944991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this is nothing to get hackles up over. If you don't like it, change it. If you change it, consider the consequences. For example, you've taken what was a privileged, narrative-driven option and dropped the entry bar significantly. And maybe that's what you need for your game, but if tone going to go that far, you could just go whole hog and erase the distinction between basic and complex entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I maybe thinking about it - in 1E <b>PtC</b> I did not clearly see very much difference between what is now Basic and Complex Refinement. Now, in light of 2E, I much more see that Complex <i>need </i>some initial experiences as Created or their world - and by this can agree with 'you need to start from Basic'. Non the less, making <i>need </i>for teacher for Complex is unnecessarily forced in rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:55:06-07:00